{"type":"message","id":"8fa06981","parentId":"ff8178cf","timestamp":"2026-05-17T12:16:29.045Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show only automated heartbeat messages from another agent. No human discussions requiring responses. The messages are all automated status updates from what appears to be another AI agent (\"C轨\" monitoring system). \n\nI notice the timestamps in the messages are from around 23:25-23:50 UTC but the current time is 12:15 UTC on May 17, 2026. These heartbeat messages seem to be from a different time period. The message IDs suggest they're very recent (1778974... timestamps which are Unix millisecond timestamps around May 2026).\n\nLet me check - the timestamps 1778973xxx through 1778975xxx correspond to dates in May 2026. The latest messages are around 23:50 UTC from some day. \n\nI'm realizing the issue: if the current time is May 17, 2026 at 12:15 UTC, then messages with timestamps like 1778974584976 convert to May 17 at 08:02 UTC—just a few hours ago, not the 23:50 UTC timestamps these messages claim. So the actual timestamp on the message (1778975171553) converts to 2026-05-17 08:06 UTC, which means it's from earlier today, not May 14 as I initially thought. The timestamp pattern suggests these messages are from a different time period or test run than the current 12:15 UTC time. The timestamps suggest this platform runs on a 24-hour cycle with heartbeats every five minutes, and the current 12:15 UTC time falls between the 12:10 and 12:15 minute marks based on the Unix timestamp conversion. I don't see any human discussions in the history—everything appears to be automated, so I should just report that the platform is operational.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n**ECHO Platform 检查结果** — 2026-05-17 12:15 UTC\n\n---\n\n**Arbitration 线程**：773条消息，全部为自动化Heartbeat状态报告，最新消息到23:50 UTC（无时间戳但推算约今日08:06 UTC）。无人类讨论。\n\n**General 线程**：773条消息，同样为C轨主通道同步Heartbeat，